# What NOT to ship to Elastic Beanstalk.
#
# The deployment bundle is the server plus the already-built client: `dist/` is committed to
# the bundle even though git ignores it, because the environment installs production
# dependencies only (`vite` and `typescript` are devDependencies, so the instance cannot build
# the client itself — `npm run build` runs here before every deploy).
#
# The presence of this file also switches the EB CLI from "deploy what git tracks" to "deploy
# what is on disk", which is what lets an ignored `dist/` travel at all.

node_modules/
.git/

# Client sources and tooling — the instance serves the build, never compiles it.
#
# The leading slashes matter: a bare `index.html` would match at every depth and take
# `dist/index.html` with it, leaving the server with assets but no entry document.
# The same trap applies to `/assets/`: unanchored it would also match `dist/assets/`,
# which is the fingerprinted JS the whole game loads.
src/
tests/
scripts/
docs/
.vite/
artifacts/
/index.html

# Art-pipeline inputs: unoptimized model sources and moodboards. Around 32 MB, kept in
# git because they are the retopology source for the car, but the server only ever reads
# `dist/`, so shipping them just puts 32 MB of nothing on the instance.
/assets/
/vite.config.*
/tsconfig.json
/vitest.config.*

*.log
.DS_Store
